§ `Part 5 -- Beneficial ownership information: the register (regulations 45, 45ZA and 45ZB)`

§§ `Regulation 45 -- Register of beneficial ownership`

-- src:1493 | (14) For the purposes of this regulation, a taxable relevant trust is a relevant trust in any year in which its trustees are liable to pay any of the following taxes in the United Kingdom in relation to assets or income of the trust—
-- src:1494 | (a) income tax;
-- src:1495 | (b) capital gains tax;
-- src:1496 | (c) inheritance tax;
-- src:1497 | (d) stamp duty land tax (within the meaning of section 42 of the Finance Act 2003 );
-- src:1498 | (e) land and buildings transaction tax (within the meaning of section 1 of the Land and Buildings Transaction Tax (Scotland) Act 2013 );
-- src:1499 | (ea) land transaction tax (within the meaning of section 2 of the Land Transaction Tax and Anti-avoidance of Devolved Taxes (Wales) Act 2017);
@ref reg 45(14) (src:1493-1499)
DECLARE `reg 45(14) tax` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45(14)(a) income tax`
    `reg 45(14)(b) capital gains tax`
    `reg 45(14)(c) inheritance tax`
    `reg 45(14)(d) stamp duty land tax (within the meaning of section 42 of the Finance`
    `reg 45(14)(e) land and buildings transaction tax (within the meaning of section 1`
    `reg 45(14)(ea) land transaction tax (within the meaning of section 2 of the Land`
    `reg 45(14) another tax`

@ref reg 45(14) (src:1493-1499)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 45(14) tax`
`reg 45(14) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 45(14)(a) income tax`
    , `reg 45(14)(b) capital gains tax`
    , `reg 45(14)(c) inheritance tax`
    , `reg 45(14)(d) stamp duty land tax (within the meaning of section 42 of the Finance`
    , `reg 45(14)(e) land and buildings transaction tax (within the meaning of section 1`
    , `reg 45(14)(ea) land transaction tax (within the meaning of section 2 of the Land`

-- reg 45(14): the taxes whose liability makes a relevant trust a taxable relevant trust (the (f) limb is blank in this text).
@ref reg 45(14) (src:1493-1499)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45(14) tax`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(14) the tax is one of the taxes` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(a) income tax` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "liable to pay any of the following taxes"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(b) capital gains tax` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "liable to pay any of the following taxes"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(c) inheritance tax` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "liable to pay any of the following taxes"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(d) stamp duty land tax (within the meaning of section 42 of the Finance` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "liable to pay any of the following taxes"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(e) land and buildings transaction tax (within the meaning of section 1` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "liable to pay any of the following taxes"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(ea) land transaction tax (within the meaning of section 2 of the Land` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "liable to pay any of the following taxes"
    WHEN `reg 45(14) another tax` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a taxable relevant trust is a relevant trust in any year in which its trustees are liable to pay any of the following taxes"; a tax in none of the heads does not make it one (a definition by a list, ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated definitions (a); fork F45-5)

@ref reg 45(14) (src:1493-1499)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45(14) tax`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 45(14) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(a) income tax` THEN JUST "income tax"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(b) capital gains tax` THEN JUST "capital gains tax"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(c) inheritance tax` THEN JUST "inheritance tax"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(d) stamp duty land tax (within the meaning of section 42 of the Finance` THEN JUST "stamp duty land tax (within the meaning of section 42 of the Finance Act 2003 )"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(e) land and buildings transaction tax (within the meaning of section 1` THEN JUST "land and buildings transaction tax (within the meaning of section 1 of the Land and Buildings Transaction Tax (Scotland) Act 2013 )"
    WHEN `reg 45(14)(ea) land transaction tax (within the meaning of section 2 of the Land` THEN JUST "land transaction tax (within the meaning of section 2 of the Land Transaction Tax and Anti-avoidance of Devolved Taxes (Wales) Act 2017)"
    WHEN `reg 45(14) another tax` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- reg 45(14): a taxable relevant trust.  A definition ("is ... in any year in which"): read like "means".
@ref reg 45(14) (src:1493-1499)
GIVEN `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the taxes that the trustees are liable to pay in the year in the United Kingdom in relation to assets or income of the trust` IS A LIST OF `reg 45(14) tax`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF any (GIVEN tax YIELD `reg 45(14) the tax is one of the taxes` tax EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the taxes that the trustees are liable to pay in the year in the United Kingdom in relation to assets or income of the trust`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a taxable relevant trust is a relevant trust in any year in which its trustees are liable to pay any of the following taxes" (no listed tax)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a taxable relevant trust is a relevant trust"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the trust is a relevant trust has not been answered

-- reg 45(1): the register.
DECLARE `reg 45(1) entry` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45(1)(a) a beneficial owner of a taxable relevant trust`
    `reg 45(1)(b) a potential beneficiary, referred to in regulation 44(5)(b), of a taxable relevant trust`
    `reg 45(1) another person`

-- src:1416 | (1) The Commissioners must maintain a register (“the register”) of—
-- src:1417 | (a) beneficial owners of taxable relevant trusts; and
-- src:1418 | (b) potential beneficiaries (referred to in regulation 44(5)(b)) of taxable relevant trusts.
@ref reg 45(1) (src:1416-1418)
GIVEN `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      entry IS A `reg 45(1) entry`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(1) the Commissioners must include the person in the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `mlr2 within the scope` `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of taxable relevant trusts"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER entry
        WHEN `reg 45(1)(a) a beneficial owner of a taxable relevant trust` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 45(1)(b) a potential beneficiary, referred to in regulation 44(5)(b), of a taxable relevant trust` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 45(1) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists (a) and (b) and does not say that the register holds no one else
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

