-- reg 45(6) and (7): the conditional items.  "if any", "if the individual does not have", "if the address ... is not in the United Kingdom" and
-- "if applicable" are the text's own conditions: when one fails, the item is not required.
-- src:1437 | (6) The information specified in this paragraph is—
-- src:1438 | (a) the individual's full name;
-- src:1439 | (b) the individual's national insurance number or unique taxpayer reference, if any;
-- src:1440 | (c) if the individual does not have a national insurance number or unique taxpayer reference, the individual's usual residential address;
-- src:1441 | (d) if the address provided under sub-paragraph (c) is not in the United Kingdom—
-- src:1442 | (i) the individual's passport number or identification card number, with the country of issue and the expiry date of the passport or identification card; or
-- src:1443 | (ii) if the individual does not have a passport or identification card, the number, country of issue and expiry date of any equivalent form of identification;
-- src:1444 | (e) the individual's date of birth;
-- src:1445 | (f) the nature of the individual's role in relation to the trust.
@ref reg 45(6) (src:1437-1445)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45(6) item`
      `the individual has a national insurance number or unique taxpayer reference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's usual residential address is in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(6) the item must be provided for the individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45(6)(a) the individual's full name` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 45(6)(b) the individual's national insurance number or unique taxpayer` THEN
        IF `the individual has a national insurance number or unique taxpayer reference` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the individual's national insurance number or unique taxpayer reference, if any"
    WHEN `reg 45(6)(c) if the individual does not have a national insurance number or unique` THEN
        IF (NOT `the individual has a national insurance number or unique taxpayer reference`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the individual does not have a national insurance number or unique taxpayer reference, the individual's usual residential address"
    WHEN `reg 45(6)(d) if the address provided under sub-paragraph (c) is not in the United` THEN
        IF (NOT `the individual has a national insurance number or unique taxpayer reference`) AND (NOT `the individual's usual residential address is in the United Kingdom`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the address provided under sub-paragraph (c) is not in the United Kingdom" (an address is provided under (c) only when there is no national insurance number or unique taxpayer reference)
    WHEN `reg 45(6)(e) the individual's date of birth` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 45(6)(f) the nature of the individual's role in relation to the trust` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 45(6) another item` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 45(2)(b) hands "the information specified in paragraph (6)" to this list, and the paragraph says "The information specified in this paragraph is"; an item in none of the heads is not specified (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated definitions (a); fork F45-4)

