      `the legal entity is entered in a register of companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(7) the item must be provided for the legal entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45(7)(a) the legal entity's corporate or firm name` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 45(7)(b) the legal entity's unique taxpayer reference, if any` THEN
        IF `the legal entity has a unique taxpayer reference` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the legal entity's unique taxpayer reference, if any"
    WHEN `reg 45(7)(c) the registered or principal office of the legal entity` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 45(7)(d) the legal form of the legal entity and the law by which it is governed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 45(7)(e) if applicable, the name of the register of companies in which the legal` THEN
        IF `the legal entity is entered in a register of companies` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if applicable, the name of the register of companies in which the legal entity is entered"
    WHEN `reg 45(7)(f) the nature of the entity's role in relation to the trust` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 45(7) another item` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 45(2)(c) hands "the information specified in paragraph (7)" to this list, and the paragraph says "The information specified in this paragraph is"; an item in none of the heads is not specified (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated definitions (a); fork F45-4)

-- reg 45(8): one item, a description of the class.  Reg 45(2)(d) and 45(10F) say when it is given.
-- src:1453 | (8) The information specified in this paragraph is a description of the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust.
@ref reg 45(8) (src:1453-1453)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 45(8) the information specified in this paragraph is` MEANS "a description of the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust"

-- reg 45(2): what the trustees of a taxable relevant trust must provide.
DECLARE `reg 45(2) information` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45(2)(a) the information specified in paragraph (5) in relation to the trust`
    `reg 45(2)(b) the information specified in paragraph (6) in relation to each of the individuals referred to in regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b)`
    `reg 45(2)(c) the information specified in paragraph (7) in relation to each of the legal entities referred to in regulation 44(2)(b)`
    `reg 45(2)(d) the information specified in paragraph (8)`

-- src:1419 | (2) The trustees of a taxable relevant trust must within the time specified in paragraph (3) provide the Commissioners with—
-- src:1420 | (a) the information specified in paragraph (5) in relation to the trust;
-- src:1421 | (b) the information specified in paragraph (6) in relation to each of the individuals referred to in regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b) (but if sub-paragraph (d) applies, this information does not need to be provided in relation to the beneficiaries of the trust);
-- src:1422 | (c) the information specified in paragraph (7) in relation to each of the legal entities referred to in regulation 44(2)(b);
-- src:1423 | (d) the information specified in paragraph (8), where the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined.
@ref reg 45(2) (src:1419-1423)
GIVEN `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      information IS A `reg 45(2) information`
      `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a beneficiary of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(2) the trustees must provide the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `mlr2 within the scope` `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustees of a taxable relevant trust must"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER information
        WHEN `reg 45(2)(a) the information specified in paragraph (5) in relation to the trust` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 45(2)(b) the information specified in paragraph (6) in relation to each of the individuals referred to in regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b)` THEN
            IF `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined` AND `the individual is a beneficiary of the trust`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but if sub-paragraph (d) applies, this information does not need to be provided in relation to the beneficiaries of the trust"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 45(2)(c) the information specified in paragraph (7) in relation to each of the legal entities referred to in regulation 44(2)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 45(2)(d) the information specified in paragraph (8)` THEN
            IF `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the information specified in paragraph (8), where the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- reg 45(3): the day by which the information must be provided.
-- "apart from any information already provided to the Commissioners under regulation 45ZA" is information the trustees need not provide again.
-- (a) a trust set up before 6 April 2021: on or before 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees were first liable.
-- (b) a trust set up after 5 April 2021 where the trustees became liable before 4 June 2022: on or before 1 September 2022.
-- (c) any other case: within 90 days of the trustees becoming liable (the 90th day after that day, fork F45-1).
-- src:1424 | (3) The information required under paragraph (2) must, apart from any information already provided to the Commissioners under regulation 45ZA (at a time when the trust was not a taxable relevant trust), be provided—
-- src:1425 | (a) on or before 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees were first liable to pay any of the taxes referred to in paragraph (14) (“UK taxes”), in the case of a trust which is set up before 6th April 2021;
-- src:1426 | (b) on or before 1st September 2022, in the case of a trust which is set up after 5th April 2021 where the trustees become liable to pay UK taxes before 4th June 2022;
-- src:1427 | (c) within 90 days of the trustees becoming liable to pay UK taxes, in any other case.
@ref reg 45(3) (src:1424-1427)
GIVEN `the date on which the trust was set up` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the trustees became liable to pay UK taxes` IS A DATE
      `the 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees were first liable to pay any of the taxes referred to in paragraph (14)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45(3) the last day for providing the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date on which the trust was set up` LESS THAN Date 6 4 2021
        THEN `the 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees were first liable to pay any of the taxes referred to in paragraph (14)`
        IF `the date on which the trustees became liable to pay UK taxes` LESS THAN Date 4 6 2022
        THEN Date 1 9 2022
        OTHERWISE `the date on which the trustees became liable to pay UK taxes` PLUS 90

-- src:1424 | (3) The information required under paragraph (2) must, apart from any information already provided to the Commissioners under regulation 45ZA (at a time when the trust was not a taxable relevant trust), be provided—
-- src:1425 | (a) on or before 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees were first liable to pay any of the taxes referred to in paragraph (14) (“UK taxes”), in the case of a trust which is set up before 6th April 2021;
-- src:1426 | (b) on or before 1st September 2022, in the case of a trust which is set up after 5th April 2021 where the trustees become liable to pay UK taxes before 4th June 2022;
-- src:1427 | (c) within 90 days of the trustees becoming liable to pay UK taxes, in any other case.
@ref reg 45(3) (src:1424-1427)
GIVEN `the date on which the information was provided` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day for providing the information` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(3) the information was provided in time` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the information was provided` `the last day for providing the information` `the date asked`

-- reg 45(4)
-- src:1428 | (4) The information required under paragraphs (2) and (9) must be provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require.
@ref reg 45(4) (src:1428-1428)
GIVEN `the information was provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(4) the information required under paragraphs (2) and (9) was provided in the form required` MEANS
    IF `the information was provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require" (a "must" not discharged, marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 45(9): changes.  "31st January after the tax year ...": days given as inputs.
-- src:1454 | (9) The trustees of a taxable relevant trust must—
-- src:1455 | (a) if a trustee becomes aware that any of the information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (2) (other than information provided in relation to the value of the trust assets under paragraph (5)(c)) has changed, notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred on or before 31st January—
-- src:1456 | (i) after the tax year in which the change occurred; or
-- src:1457 | (ii) if the trustees are not liable to pay any UK taxes in that year, after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes; or
-- src:1458 | (b) if the trustees are not aware of any change to any of the information provided under paragraph (2), confirm that fact to the Commissioners on or before 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes.
@ref reg 45(9) (src:1454-1458)
GIVEN `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a trustee becomes aware that information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (2) has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information that has changed is the value of the trust assets provided under paragraph (5)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(9)(a) the trustees must notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred` MEANS
    CONSIDER `mlr2 within the scope` `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustees of a taxable relevant trust must"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH
            IF (NOT `a trustee becomes aware that information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (2) has changed`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a trustee becomes aware that any of the information ... has changed, notify the Commissioners" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)
            IF `the information that has changed is the value of the trust assets provided under paragraph (5)(c)`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(other than information provided in relation to the value of the trust assets under paragraph (5)(c))"
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The last day for the notice: "on or before 31st January (i) after the tax year in which the change occurred; or (ii) if the trustees are
-- not liable to pay any UK taxes in that year, after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes".
-- src:1455 | (a) if a trustee becomes aware that any of the information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (2) (other than information provided in relation to the value of the trust assets under paragraph (5)(c)) has changed, notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred on or before 31st January—
-- src:1456 | (i) after the tax year in which the change occurred; or
-- src:1457 | (ii) if the trustees are not liable to pay any UK taxes in that year, after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes; or
@ref reg 45(9)(a) (src:1455-1457)
GIVEN `the trustees are liable to pay UK taxes in the tax year in which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the 31st January after the tax year in which the change occurred` IS A DATE
      `the 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45(9)(a) the last day for notifying the change` MEANS
    IF `the trustees are liable to pay UK taxes in the tax year in which the change occurred`
    THEN `the 31st January after the tax year in which the change occurred`
    ELSE `the 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes`

-- src:1455 | (a) if a trustee becomes aware that any of the information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (2) (other than information provided in relation to the value of the trust assets under paragraph (5)(c)) has changed, notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred on or before 31st January—
-- src:1456 | (i) after the tax year in which the change occurred; or
-- src:1457 | (ii) if the trustees are not liable to pay any UK taxes in that year, after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes; or
@ref reg 45(9)(a) (src:1455-1457)
GIVEN `the date on which the change was notified` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day for notifying the change` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(9)(a) the change was notified in time` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the change was notified` `the last day for notifying the change` `the date asked`

-- src:1458 | (b) if the trustees are not aware of any change to any of the information provided under paragraph (2), confirm that fact to the Commissioners on or before 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes.
@ref reg 45(9)(b) (src:1458-1458)
GIVEN `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustees are not aware of any change to any of the information provided under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(9)(b) the trustees must confirm to the Commissioners that there is no change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `mlr2 within the scope` `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustees of a taxable relevant trust must"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the trustees are not aware of any change to any of the information provided under paragraph (2)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the trustees are not aware of any change ..., confirm that fact" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:1458 | (b) if the trustees are not aware of any change to any of the information provided under paragraph (2), confirm that fact to the Commissioners on or before 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes.
@ref reg 45(9)(b) (src:1458-1458)
GIVEN `the date on which the trustees confirmed that there is no change` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(9)(b) the confirmation was given in time` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the trustees confirmed that there is no change` `the 31st January after the tax year in which the trustees are liable to pay any UK taxes` `the date asked`

-- reg 45(10): what the register contains.
DECLARE `reg 45(10) kind of trust` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45(10)(a) a taxable relevant trust`
    `reg 45(10)(b) a taxable relevant trust of a type mentioned in paragraphs (10A) to (10C)`
    `reg 45(10)(c) a trust of a type mentioned in regulation 45ZA(1)`

DECLARE `reg 45(10) kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45(10) the information referred to in regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b)`
    `reg 45(10) the information referred to in paragraphs (10E) to (10G)`
    `reg 45(10) the information referred to in regulation 45ZA(3) and (4)`

-- src:1459 | (10) The register must contain the information referred to in—
-- src:1460 | (a) regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b), in relation to taxable relevant trusts;
-- src:1461 | (b) regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b) and paragraphs (10E) to (10G), in relation to the types of taxable relevant trust mentioned in paragraphs (10A) to (10C);
-- src:1462 | (c) regulation 45ZA(3) and (4), in relation to the types of trust mentioned in regulation 45ZA(1).
@ref reg 45(10) (src:1459-1462)
GIVEN trust IS A `reg 45(10) kind of trust`
      information IS A `reg 45(10) kind of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10) the register must contain the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER trust
    WHEN `reg 45(10)(a) a taxable relevant trust` THEN
        CONSIDER information
        WHEN `reg 45(10) the information referred to in regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 45(10) the information referred to in paragraphs (10E) to (10G)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): sub-paragraph (a) names regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b) only, and sub-paragraph (b) adds paragraphs (10E) to (10G) for the types in (10A) to (10C)
        WHEN `reg 45(10) the information referred to in regulation 45ZA(3) and (4)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): sub-paragraph (c) is for the types in regulation 45ZA(1)
    WHEN `reg 45(10)(b) a taxable relevant trust of a type mentioned in paragraphs (10A) to (10C)` THEN
        CONSIDER information
        WHEN `reg 45(10) the information referred to in regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 45(10) the information referred to in paragraphs (10E) to (10G)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 45(10) the information referred to in regulation 45ZA(3) and (4)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): sub-paragraph (c) is for the types in regulation 45ZA(1)
    WHEN `reg 45(10)(c) a trust of a type mentioned in regulation 45ZA(1)` THEN
        CONSIDER information
        WHEN `reg 45(10) the information referred to in regulation 44(2)(b) and (5)(b)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): sub-paragraph (c) names regulation 45ZA(3) and (4) only
        WHEN `reg 45(10) the information referred to in paragraphs (10E) to (10G)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): sub-paragraph (c) names regulation 45ZA(3) and (4) only
        WHEN `reg 45(10) the information referred to in regulation 45ZA(3) and (4)` THEN JUST TRUE

-- reg 45(10A), (10B), (10C): the trusts they concern.  Each opens a described class ("which is", "This paragraph applies to"): outside it the paragraph is silent.
-- SEAM S-18 (asking)
-- src:1463 | (10A) The trustees of a taxable relevant trust which is a UK trust, and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust listed in Schedule 3A, must provide the Commissioners with the information specified in paragraph (10E), apart from any information already provided to the Commissioners under regulation 45ZA (at a time when the trust was not a taxable relevant trust)—
-- src:1464 | (a) on or before 1st September 2022, where the trustees become liable to pay UK taxes before 4th June 2022;
-- src:1465 | (b) within 90 days of the trustees becoming liable to pay UK taxes, in any other case.
@ref reg 45(10A) (src:1463-1465)
GIVEN `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(4) the trust is an EEA registered trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10A) paragraph (10A) applies to the trustees` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year`
        (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust`
            (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 42(4) the trust is an EEA registered trust`) (`mlr2 the opposite of` `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`)))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The trustees of a taxable relevant trust which is a UK trust, and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust listed in Schedule 3A" -- paragraphs (10D), (10G) and (10H) turn on whether paragraph (10A), (10B) or (10C) "applies", so the class each describes is read as the whole of its application: a trust outside it is one to which the paragraph does not apply (fork F45-6)

-- src:1463 | (10A) The trustees of a taxable relevant trust which is a UK trust, and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust listed in Schedule 3A, must provide the Commissioners with the information specified in paragraph (10E), apart from any information already provided to the Commissioners under regulation 45ZA (at a time when the trust was not a taxable relevant trust)—
-- src:1464 | (a) on or before 1st September 2022, where the trustees become liable to pay UK taxes before 4th June 2022;
-- src:1465 | (b) within 90 days of the trustees becoming liable to pay UK taxes, in any other case.
@ref reg 45(10A) (src:1463-1465)
GIVEN `the date on which the trustees became liable to pay UK taxes` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45(10A) the last day for providing the information` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the trustees became liable to pay UK taxes` LESS THAN Date 4 6 2022
    THEN Date 1 9 2022
    ELSE `the date on which the trustees became liable to pay UK taxes` PLUS 90

-- SEAM S-18 (asking)
-- src:1466 | (10B) This paragraph applies to the trustees of a taxable relevant trust which is a non-UK trust, has at least one trustee resident in the United Kingdom and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust falling within Schedule 3A, where the trustees of that trust, in their capacity as such—
-- src:1467 | (a) enter into a business relationship with a relevant person; or
-- src:1468 | (b) acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 45(10B) (src:1466-1468)
GIVEN `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(2)(e) the trust is a non-UK trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `at least one trustee is resident in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(4) the trust is an EEA registered trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustees enter into a business relationship with a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10B) paragraph (10B) applies to the trustees` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year`
        (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 42(2)(e) the trust is a non-UK trust`
            (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `at least one trustee is resident in the United Kingdom`)
                (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 42(4) the trust is an EEA registered trust`)
                    (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`)
                        (`mlr2 the fact stated` (`the trustees enter into a business relationship with a relevant person` OR `the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom`))))))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph applies to the trustees of a taxable relevant trust which is a non-UK trust, has at least one trustee resident in the United Kingdom and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust falling within Schedule 3A, where the trustees ... (a) enter into a business relationship with a relevant person; or (b) acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom" -- the "where" fails when neither happens (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)); a trust outside the described class is one to which the paragraph does not apply (fork F45-6)

-- src:1469 | (10C) This paragraph applies to the trustees of a taxable relevant trust which is a non-UK trust and is not a trust listed in Schedule 3A, where none of the trustees are resident in the United Kingdom and those trustees, in their capacity as such, acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 45(10C) (src:1469-1469)
GIVEN `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(2)(e) the trust is a non-UK trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `none of the trustees is resident in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10C) paragraph (10C) applies to the trustees` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year`
        (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 42(2)(e) the trust is a non-UK trust`
            (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`)
                (`mlr2 the fact stated` (`none of the trustees is resident in the United Kingdom` AND `the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom`))))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph applies to the trustees of a taxable relevant trust which is a non-UK trust and is not a trust listed in Schedule 3A, where none of the trustees are resident in the United Kingdom and those trustees ... acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom" -- the "where" fails when a trustee is resident or no interest in land is acquired (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)); a trust outside the described class is one to which the paragraph does not apply (fork F45-6)

-- reg 45(10D): the day by which the (10E) information is due.  (a) 1 September 2022 where the trustees became liable before 4 June 2022; (b) otherwise within 90 days of
-- acquiring the land or, where (10B)(a) applies, of entering into the business relationship.
-- src:1470 | (10D) Where paragraph (10B) or (10C) applies, the trustees must provide the Commissioners with the information specified in paragraph (10E), apart from any information already provided to the Commissioners under regulation 45ZA (at a time when the trust was not a taxable relevant trust)—
-- src:1471 | (a) on or before 1st September 2022, where the trustees become liable to pay UK taxes before 4th June 2022;
-- src:1472 | (b) otherwise, within 90 days of the trustees acquiring the land or (where paragraph (10B)(a) applies) entering into the business relationship.
@ref reg 45(10D) (src:1470-1472)
GIVEN `the date on which the trustees became liable to pay UK taxes` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the trustees acquired the land or, where paragraph (10B)(a) applies, entered into the business relationship` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45(10D) the last day for providing the information` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the trustees became liable to pay UK taxes` LESS THAN Date 4 6 2022
    THEN Date 1 9 2022
    ELSE `the date on which the trustees acquired the land or, where paragraph (10B)(a) applies, entered into the business relationship` PLUS 90

-- (10D) duty: "Where paragraph (10B) or (10C) applies, the trustees must provide ...".
-- src:1470 | (10D) Where paragraph (10B) or (10C) applies, the trustees must provide the Commissioners with the information specified in paragraph (10E), apart from any information already provided to the Commissioners under regulation 45ZA (at a time when the trust was not a taxable relevant trust)—
@ref reg 45(10D) (src:1470-1470)
GIVEN `reg 45(10B) paragraph (10B) applies to the trustees` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 45(10C) paragraph (10C) applies to the trustees` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10D) the trustees must provide the Commissioners with the information specified in paragraph (10E)` MEANS
    `mlr2 either is true` `reg 45(10B) paragraph (10B) applies to the trustees` `reg 45(10C) paragraph (10C) applies to the trustees`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where paragraph (10B) or (10C) applies, the trustees must provide" -- a "where" that fails: neither applies (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:1473 | (10E) The trustees must provide the Commissioners with the following information in relation to each of the beneficial owners of the trust who is an individual, and in relation to any other individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes—
-- src:1474 | (a) the individual’s country of residence;
-- src:1475 | (b) the individual’s nationality;
-- src:1476 | (c) the nature and extent of the individual’s beneficial interest,
-- src:1477 | but if paragraph (10F) applies, this information does not need to be provided in relation to the beneficiaries of the trust.
@ref reg 45(10E) (src:1473-1477)
