    WHEN `reg 45(10E)(a) the individual's country of residence` THEN JUST "the individual’s country of residence"
    WHEN `reg 45(10E)(b) the individual's nationality` THEN JUST "the individual’s nationality"
    WHEN `reg 45(10E)(c) the nature and extent of the individual's beneficial interest` THEN JUST "the nature and extent of the individual’s beneficial interest"
    WHEN `reg 45(10E) another item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- reg 45(10E) and (10F): the beneficiaries.
-- src:1473 | (10E) The trustees must provide the Commissioners with the following information in relation to each of the beneficial owners of the trust who is an individual, and in relation to any other individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes—
-- src:1474 | (a) the individual’s country of residence;
-- src:1475 | (b) the individual’s nationality;
-- src:1476 | (c) the nature and extent of the individual’s beneficial interest,
-- src:1477 | but if paragraph (10F) applies, this information does not need to be provided in relation to the beneficiaries of the trust.
-- src:1478 | (10F) Where the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined, the information to be provided under paragraph (10E) is a description of the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust.
@ref reg 45(10E) (src:1473-1478)
GIVEN `paragraph (10F) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10E) the information must be provided in relation to the beneficiaries of the trust` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (10F) applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but if paragraph (10F) applies, this information does not need to be provided in relation to the beneficiaries of the trust"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is of the case in which paragraph (10F) applies; for the other case the paragraph says that the information is to be provided in relation to each individual beneficial owner

-- src:1478 | (10F) Where the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined, the information to be provided under paragraph (10E) is a description of the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust.
@ref reg 45(10F) (src:1478-1478)
GIVEN `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
