-- reg 45(10G): the third country entity.  (a) with the (10E) information; (b) within 90 days of acquiring the interest, if acquired afterwards.
-- SEAM S-18 (asking)
-- src:1479 | (10G) The trustees of a trust to which paragraph (10A) , (10B) or (10C) applies must—
-- src:1480 | (a) if they have a controlling interest in a third country entity, provide the Commissioners with the following information, apart from any information already provided under regulation 45ZA(4), at the same time as providing the information under paragraph (10E)—
-- src:1481 | (i) the third country entity’s corporate or firm name;
-- src:1482 | (ii) the country or territory by whose law the third country entity is governed;
-- src:1483 | (iii) the registered or principal office of the third country entity;
-- src:1484 | (b) if they acquire an interest in a third country entity after providing the information under paragraph (10E), provide the Commissioners with the information specified in this paragraph within 90 days of the date on which they acquired that interest.
@ref reg 45(10G) (src:1479-1484)
GIVEN `reg 45(10A) paragraph (10A) applies to the trustees` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 45(10B) paragraph (10B) applies to the trustees` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 45(10C) paragraph (10C) applies to the trustees` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(6)(a) the trustees have a controlling interest in a third country entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustees acquire an interest in a third country entity after providing the information under paragraph (10E)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10G) the trustees must provide the Commissioners with the information about the third country entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `mlr2 within the scope` (`mlr2 either is true` `reg 45(10A) paragraph (10A) applies to the trustees` (`mlr2 either is true` `reg 45(10B) paragraph (10B) applies to the trustees` `reg 45(10C) paragraph (10C) applies to the trustees`)) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustees of a trust to which paragraph (10A), (10B) or (10C) applies"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `reg 42(6)(a) the trustees have a controlling interest in a third country entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the trustees acquire an interest in a third country entity after providing the information under paragraph (10E)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if they have a controlling interest in a third country entity, provide ...; (b) if they acquire an interest in a third country entity after providing the information under paragraph (10E), provide" (an "if" that fails: neither (a) nor (b) is met)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:1484 | (b) if they acquire an interest in a third country entity after providing the information under paragraph (10E), provide the Commissioners with the information specified in this paragraph within 90 days of the date on which they acquired that interest.
@ref reg 45(10G)(b) (src:1484-1484)
GIVEN `the date on which the trustees acquired the interest in the third country entity` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45(10G)(b) the last day for providing the information` MEANS `the date on which the trustees acquired the interest in the third country entity` PLUS 90

-- reg 45(10H): a change, within 90 days of the trustee becoming aware.
-- src:1485 | (10H) The trustees of a taxable relevant trust to which paragraph (10A), (10B) or (10C) applies must, if the trustee becomes aware that any of the information provided to the Commissioners under paragraphs (10E) to (10G) has changed, notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred within 90 days of the trustee becoming aware of the change.
@ref reg 45(10H) (src:1485-1485)
GIVEN `reg 45(10H) paragraph (10A), (10B) or (10C) applies to the trustees` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustee becomes aware that information provided to the Commissioners under paragraphs (10E) to (10G) has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10H) the trustees must notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred` MEANS
    CONSIDER `mlr2 within the scope` `reg 45(10H) paragraph (10A), (10B) or (10C) applies to the trustees` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustees of a taxable relevant trust to which paragraph (10A), (10B) or (10C) applies"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the trustee becomes aware that information provided to the Commissioners under paragraphs (10E) to (10G) has changed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the trustee becomes aware that any of the information ... has changed" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:1485 | (10H) The trustees of a taxable relevant trust to which paragraph (10A), (10B) or (10C) applies must, if the trustee becomes aware that any of the information provided to the Commissioners under paragraphs (10E) to (10G) has changed, notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred within 90 days of the trustee becoming aware of the change.
@ref reg 45(10H) (src:1485-1485)
GIVEN `the date on which the trustee became aware of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45(10H) the last day for the notification` MEANS `the date on which the trustee became aware of the change` PLUS 90

-- src:1485 | (10H) The trustees of a taxable relevant trust to which paragraph (10A), (10B) or (10C) applies must, if the trustee becomes aware that any of the information provided to the Commissioners under paragraphs (10E) to (10G) has changed, notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred within 90 days of the trustee becoming aware of the change.
@ref reg 45(10H) (src:1485-1485)
GIVEN `the date on which the notification was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the trustee became aware of the change` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10H) the notification was given within 90 days` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the notification was given` (`reg 45(10H) the last day for the notification` `the date on which the trustee became aware of the change`) `the date asked`

DECLARE `reg 45(10H) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45(10H) the trustees of a taxable relevant trust`

DECLARE `reg 45(10H) act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45(10H) notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred`

@ref reg 45(10H) (src:1485-1485)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 45(10H) party` `reg 45(10H) act`
`reg 45(10H) the trustees must notify the Commissioners within 90 days` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 45(10H) the trustees of a taxable relevant trust`
    MUST `reg 45(10H) notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred`
    WITHIN 90
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the trustees did not notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred within 90 days of the trustee becoming aware of the change"

-- reg 45(10I)
-- src:1486 | (10I) The information required under paragraphs (10E) to (10H) must be provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require.
@ref reg 45(10I) (src:1486-1486)
GIVEN `the information was provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
