    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require" (a "must" not discharged, marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 45(10J): at least five years, and no more than 10 years, after the trust ceased to exist or ceased to be a type of trust in paragraph (10).
-- The paragraph fixes a floor (five years) and a ceiling (10 years).  "Must keep" is the floor: yes up to the fifth anniversary, no after it, as for regulation 40(1) ("at least the period").
-- "May keep" is the ceiling: yes up to the tenth anniversary, no after it.  Both fix a period in the text's own words (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); fork F45-3).
-- src:1487 | (10J) The Commissioners must keep the information referred to in paragraph (10) on the register for at least five years, and no more than 10 years, after the trust to which it relates has ceased to exist or has ceased to be a type of trust referred to in paragraph (10).
@ref reg 45(10J) (src:1487-1487)
GIVEN `the date on which the trust ceased to exist or ceased to be a type of trust referred to in paragraph (10)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10J) the Commissioners must keep the information on the register on the date asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the trust ceased to exist or ceased to be a type of trust referred to in paragraph (10)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph counts from the day the trust ceased to exist or ceased to be a type of trust in paragraph (10), and that day has not come
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN
        IF `the date asked` AT MOST `add years` ceased 5
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for at least five years, and no more than 10 years, after the trust ... has ceased" -- the duty to keep runs for the five years the text fixes in its own words; after them the Commissioners are not required to keep the information (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); consistent with regulation 40(1))

@ref reg 45(10J) (src:1487-1487)
GIVEN `the date on which the trust ceased to exist or ceased to be a type of trust referred to in paragraph (10)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(10J) the Commissioners may keep the information on the register on the date asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the trust ceased to exist or ceased to be a type of trust referred to in paragraph (10)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph counts from the day the trust ceased to exist or ceased to be a type of trust in paragraph (10), and that day has not come
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN
        IF `the date asked` AT MOST `add years` ceased 10
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no more than 10 years, after the trust to which it relates has ceased to exist" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

