      `the person is a trustee of the taxable relevant trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the manager or operator of the collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45(15) the person is within the reference to the trustees of the taxable relevant trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a trustee of the taxable relevant trust` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the taxable relevant trust is a collective investment scheme` AND `the person is the manager or operator of the collective investment scheme` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to the trustees of a taxable relevant trust includes a reference to the manager or operator of the collective investment scheme"

§§ `Regulation 45ZA -- Register of beneficial ownership: additional types of trust`

-- reg 45ZA(2): type A, type B and type C trusts.  The dates "on which this paragraph comes into force" (lines 1513 and 1516) are inputs.
-- A definition ("a 'type A trust' is"): read like "means".  Facts about the trust are the record of regulation 42(2)(b), asked once.
-- SEAM S-18 (asking)
-- src:1508 | (2) For the purposes of this regulation—
@ref reg 45ZA(2) (src:1508-1508)
-- src:1509 | (a) a “type A trust” is a UK trust which is an express trust and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust listed in Schedule 3A;
@ref reg 45ZA(2)(a) (src:1509-1509)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 42(2)(b) the trust`
      `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(4) the trust is an EEA registered trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(2)(a) the trust is a type A trust` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` (facts's `the trust is an express trust`))
        (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust`
            (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 42(4) the trust is an EEA registered trust`) (`mlr2 the opposite of` `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`)))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'type A trust' is a UK trust which is an express trust and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust listed in Schedule 3A" (passed through from the answers it is made of)

-- (b)(iii) and (c)(ii): "acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including
-- the date on which this paragraph comes into force".  NOTHING for the last day held means the trustees still hold it.
-- src:1510 | (b) a “type B trust” is a non-UK trust which has at least one trustee resident in the United Kingdom, is an express trust and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust listed in Schedule 3A, where the trustees of that trust, in their capacity as such—
-- src:1511 | (i) enter into a business relationship with a relevant person; ...
-- src:1512 | (ii) acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom; or
-- src:1513 | (iii) acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including the date on which this paragraph comes into force;
@ref reg 45ZA(2)(b) (src:1510-1513)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 42(2)(b) the trust`
      `reg 45ZA(2)(b)(iii) the date on which this paragraph comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(2)(b)(iii) the trustees acquired an interest in land before 6 October 2020 and continued to hold it up to the commencement date` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the date on which the trustees acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020" (no acquisition)
    WHEN JUST acquired THEN
        IF acquired LESS THAN Date 6 10 2020 AND `held up to and including the commencement date`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "acquired ... before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including the date on which this paragraph comes into force"
    WHERE
        `held up to and including the commencement date` MEANS
            CONSIDER facts's `the last day on which the trustees held that interest`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST last THEN last AT LEAST `reg 45ZA(2)(b)(iii) the date on which this paragraph comes into force`

-- src:1514 | (c) a “type C trust” is a non-UK trust which is an express trust and is not a trust listed in Schedule 3A, where none of the trustees are resident in the United Kingdom and those trustees, in their capacity as such—
-- src:1515 | (i) acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom, or
-- src:1516 | (ii) acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including the date on which this paragraph comes into force.
@ref reg 45ZA(2)(c) (src:1514-1516)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 42(2)(b) the trust`
      `reg 45ZA(2)(c)(ii) the date on which this paragraph comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(2)(c)(ii) the trustees acquired an interest in land before 6 October 2020 and continued to hold it up to the commencement date` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the date on which the trustees acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020" (no acquisition)
    WHEN JUST acquired THEN
        IF acquired LESS THAN Date 6 10 2020 AND `held up to and including the commencement date`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "acquired ... before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including the date on which this paragraph comes into force"
    WHERE
        `held up to and including the commencement date` MEANS
            CONSIDER facts's `the last day on which the trustees held that interest`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST last THEN last AT LEAST `reg 45ZA(2)(c)(ii) the date on which this paragraph comes into force`

-- SEAM S-18 (asking)
-- src:1510 | (b) a “type B trust” is a non-UK trust which has at least one trustee resident in the United Kingdom, is an express trust and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust listed in Schedule 3A, where the trustees of that trust, in their capacity as such—
-- src:1511 | (i) enter into a business relationship with a relevant person; ...
-- src:1512 | (ii) acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom; or
-- src:1513 | (iii) acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including the date on which this paragraph comes into force;
@ref reg 45ZA(2)(b) (src:1510-1513)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 42(2)(b) the trust`
      `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(4) the trust is an EEA registered trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 45ZA(2)(b)(iii) the date on which this paragraph comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(2)(b) the trust is a type B trust` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` (facts's `the trust is an express trust`))
        (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust`)
            (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` (facts's `at least one of the trustees is resident in the United Kingdom`))
                (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 42(4) the trust is an EEA registered trust`)
                    (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`)
                        (`mlr2 either is true` (facts's `the trustees enter into a business relationship with a relevant person`)
                            (`mlr2 either is true` (facts's `the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom`)
                                (`reg 45ZA(2)(b)(iii) the trustees acquired an interest in land before 6 October 2020 and continued to hold it up to the commencement date` facts `reg 45ZA(2)(b)(iii) the date on which this paragraph comes into force`)))))))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'type B trust' is a non-UK trust which has at least one trustee resident in the United Kingdom, is an express trust and is not an EEA registered trust or a trust listed in Schedule 3A, where the trustees ... (i) enter into a business relationship ...; (ii) acquire an interest in land ...; or (iii) acquired an interest in land ... before 6th October 2020" (passed through from the answers it is made of)

-- src:1514 | (c) a “type C trust” is a non-UK trust which is an express trust and is not a trust listed in Schedule 3A, where none of the trustees are resident in the United Kingdom and those trustees, in their capacity as such—
-- src:1515 | (i) acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom, or
-- src:1516 | (ii) acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including the date on which this paragraph comes into force.
@ref reg 45ZA(2)(c) (src:1514-1516)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 42(2)(b) the trust`
      `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 45ZA(2)(c)(ii) the date on which this paragraph comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(2)(c) the trust is a type C trust` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` (facts's `the trust is an express trust`))
        (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust`)
            (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`)
                (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` (NOT facts's `at least one of the trustees is resident in the United Kingdom`))
                    (`mlr2 either is true` (facts's `the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom`)
                        (`reg 45ZA(2)(c)(ii) the trustees acquired an interest in land before 6 October 2020 and continued to hold it up to the commencement date` facts `reg 45ZA(2)(c)(ii) the date on which this paragraph comes into force`)))))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'type C trust' is a non-UK trust which is an express trust and is not a trust listed in Schedule 3A, where none of the trustees are resident in the United Kingdom and those trustees ... (i) acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom, or (ii) acquired an interest in land ... before 6th October 2020" (passed through from the answers it is made of)

-- reg 45ZA(1): the trusts whose register entry is the information in paragraphs (3) and (4): types A, B, C "other than taxable relevant trusts".
-- src:1503 | (1) In relation to trusts which are—
-- src:1504 | (a) type A trusts, other than taxable relevant trusts;
-- src:1505 | (b) type B trusts, other than taxable relevant trusts;
-- src:1506 | (c) type C trusts, other than taxable relevant trusts,
-- src:1507 | the information to be contained in the register maintained under this Part is the information referred to in paragraphs (3) and (4), and in this paragraph, “taxable relevant trust” has the meaning given in regulation 45.
@ref reg 45ZA(1) (src:1503-1507)
GIVEN `reg 45ZA(2)(a) the trust is a type A trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 45ZA(2)(b) the trust is a type B trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 45ZA(2)(c) the trust is a type C trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(1) the information to be contained in the register is the information referred to in paragraphs (3) and (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 45(14) the trust is a taxable relevant trust in the year`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "type A trusts, other than taxable relevant trusts"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `mlr2 either is true` `reg 45ZA(2)(a) the trust is a type A trust` (`mlr2 either is true` `reg 45ZA(2)(b) the trust is a type B trust` `reg 45ZA(2)(c) the trust is a type C trust`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the trust is a taxable relevant trust has not been answered

-- reg 45ZA(3): who provides what, and (b) the class.  Gate: "The trustees of a trust to which paragraph (1) applies".
-- src:1518 | (a) the information specified in paragraphs (i) to (v) in relation to each of the beneficial owners of the trust who is an individual, and in relation to any other individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes—
-- src:1519 | (i) the individual’s full name;
-- src:1520 | (ii) the individual’s month and year of birth;
-- src:1521 | (iii) the individual’s country of residence;
-- src:1522 | (iv) the individual’s nationality;
-- src:1523 | (v) the nature and extent of the individual’s beneficial interest,
-- src:1524 | but if sub-paragraph (b) applies, this information does not need to be provided in relation to the beneficiaries of the trust;
@ref reg 45ZA(3)(a) (src:1518-1524)
DECLARE `reg 45ZA(3)(a) item` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(i) the individual's full name`
    `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(ii) the individual's month and year of birth`
    `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(iii) the individual's country of residence`
    `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(iv) the individual's nationality`
    `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(v) the nature and extent of the individual's beneficial interest`
    `reg 45ZA(3)(a) another item`

@ref reg 45ZA(3)(a) (src:1518-1524)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 45ZA(3)(a) item`
`reg 45ZA(3)(a) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(i) the individual's full name`
    , `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(ii) the individual's month and year of birth`
    , `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(iii) the individual's country of residence`
    , `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(iv) the individual's nationality`
    , `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(v) the nature and extent of the individual's beneficial interest`

-- reg 45ZA(3)(a): the information about each individual beneficial owner or potential beneficiary.
@ref reg 45ZA(3)(a) (src:1518-1524)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZA(3)(a) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(3)(a) the item is information about an individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(i) the individual's full name` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(ii) the individual's month and year of birth` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(iii) the individual's country of residence` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(iv) the individual's nationality` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(v) the nature and extent of the individual's beneficial interest` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a) another item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sub-paragraph lists the information and does not say that nothing else is required

@ref reg 45ZA(3)(a) (src:1518-1524)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZA(3)(a) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 45ZA(3)(a) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(i) the individual's full name` THEN JUST "the individual’s full name"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(ii) the individual's month and year of birth` THEN JUST "the individual’s month and year of birth"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(iii) the individual's country of residence` THEN JUST "the individual’s country of residence"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(iv) the individual's nationality` THEN JUST "the individual’s nationality"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a)(v) the nature and extent of the individual's beneficial interest` THEN JUST "the nature and extent of the individual’s beneficial interest"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(a) another item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- src:1526 | (c) the information specified in paragraphs (i) to (iii) in relation to each of the beneficial owners of the trust who is a legal entity—
-- src:1527 | (i) the legal entity’s corporate or firm name;
-- src:1528 | (ii) the registered or principal office of the legal entity;
-- src:1529 | (iii) the nature of the entity’s role in relation to the trust.
@ref reg 45ZA(3)(c) (src:1526-1529)
DECLARE `reg 45ZA(3)(c) item` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(i) the legal entity's corporate or firm name`
    `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(ii) the registered or principal office of the legal entity`
    `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(iii) the nature of the entity's role in relation to the trust`
    `reg 45ZA(3)(c) another item`

@ref reg 45ZA(3)(c) (src:1526-1529)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 45ZA(3)(c) item`
`reg 45ZA(3)(c) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(i) the legal entity's corporate or firm name`
    , `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(ii) the registered or principal office of the legal entity`
    , `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(iii) the nature of the entity's role in relation to the trust`

-- reg 45ZA(3)(c): the information about each beneficial owner that is a legal entity.
@ref reg 45ZA(3)(c) (src:1526-1529)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZA(3)(c) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(3)(c) the item is information about a legal entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(i) the legal entity's corporate or firm name` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(ii) the registered or principal office of the legal entity` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(iii) the nature of the entity's role in relation to the trust` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(c) another item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sub-paragraph lists the information and does not say that nothing else is required

@ref reg 45ZA(3)(c) (src:1526-1529)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZA(3)(c) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 45ZA(3)(c) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(i) the legal entity's corporate or firm name` THEN JUST "the legal entity’s corporate or firm name"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(ii) the registered or principal office of the legal entity` THEN JUST "the registered or principal office of the legal entity"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(c)(iii) the nature of the entity's role in relation to the trust` THEN JUST "the nature of the entity’s role in relation to the trust"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(3)(c) another item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- src:1517 | (3) The trustees of a trust to which paragraph (1) applies must, within the time specified in paragraph (5), provide the Commissioners with the following information, apart from any information already provided to the Commissioners under regulation 45 (at a time when the trust was a taxable relevant trust within the meaning of that regulation)—
-- src:1518 | (a) the information specified in paragraphs (i) to (v) in relation to each of the beneficial owners of the trust who is an individual, and in relation to any other individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes—
-- src:1519 | (i) the individual’s full name;
-- src:1520 | (ii) the individual’s month and year of birth;
-- src:1521 | (iii) the individual’s country of residence;
-- src:1522 | (iv) the individual’s nationality;
-- src:1523 | (v) the nature and extent of the individual’s beneficial interest,
-- src:1524 | but if sub-paragraph (b) applies, this information does not need to be provided in relation to the beneficiaries of the trust;
-- src:1525 | (b) where the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined, a description of the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust;
-- src:1526 | (c) the information specified in paragraphs (i) to (iii) in relation to each of the beneficial owners of the trust who is a legal entity—
-- src:1527 | (i) the legal entity’s corporate or firm name;
-- src:1528 | (ii) the registered or principal office of the legal entity;
-- src:1529 | (iii) the nature of the entity’s role in relation to the trust.
@ref reg 45ZA(3) (src:1517-1529)
GIVEN `reg 45ZA(1) the information to be contained in the register is the information referred to in paragraphs (3) and (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a beneficiary of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(3)(a) the trustees must provide the information about the individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER `mlr2 within the scope` `reg 45ZA(1) the information to be contained in the register is the information referred to in paragraphs (3) and (4)` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustees of a trust to which paragraph (1) applies must"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined` AND `the individual is a beneficiary of the trust`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but if sub-paragraph (b) applies, this information does not need to be provided in relation to the beneficiaries of the trust"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:1525 | (b) where the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined, a description of the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust;
@ref reg 45ZA(3) (src:1525-1525)
GIVEN `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 45ZA(3)(b) the information to be provided is` MEANS
    IF `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined`
    THEN JUST "a description of the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a description cannot carry JUST FALSE; the "where" that fails is answered no by the yes/no function below

-- src:1525 | (b) where the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined, a description of the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust;
@ref reg 45ZA(3)(b) (src:1525-1525)
GIVEN `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(3)(b) the information to be provided is the description of the class` MEANS
    IF `the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the beneficial owners include a class of beneficiaries, not all of whom have been determined" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:1531 | (a) if they have a controlling interest in a third country entity, provide the Commissioners with the following information, apart from any information already provided under regulation 45(10G), at the same time as providing the information under paragraph (3)—
-- src:1532 | (i) the third country entity’s corporate or firm name;
-- src:1533 | (ii) the country or territory by whose law the third country entity is governed;
-- src:1534 | (iii) the registered or principal office of the third country entity;
@ref reg 45ZA(4)(a) (src:1531-1534)
DECLARE `reg 45ZA(4)(a) item` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(i) the third country entity's corporate or firm name`
    `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(ii) the country or territory by whose law the third country entity`
    `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(iii) the registered or principal office of the third country entity`
    `reg 45ZA(4)(a) another item`

@ref reg 45ZA(4)(a) (src:1531-1534)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 45ZA(4)(a) item`
`reg 45ZA(4)(a) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(i) the third country entity's corporate or firm name`
    , `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(ii) the country or territory by whose law the third country entity`
    , `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(iii) the registered or principal office of the third country entity`

-- reg 45ZA(4)(a): the information about a third country entity in which the trustees have a controlling interest.
@ref reg 45ZA(4)(a) (src:1531-1534)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZA(4)(a) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(4)(a) the item is information about the third country entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(i) the third country entity's corporate or firm name` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(ii) the country or territory by whose law the third country entity` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(iii) the registered or principal office of the third country entity` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "provide the Commissioners with the following information"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(4)(a) another item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sub-paragraph lists the information and does not say that nothing else is required

@ref reg 45ZA(4)(a) (src:1531-1534)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZA(4)(a) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 45ZA(4)(a) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(i) the third country entity's corporate or firm name` THEN JUST "the third country entity’s corporate or firm name"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(ii) the country or territory by whose law the third country entity` THEN JUST "the country or territory by whose law the third country entity is governed"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(4)(a)(iii) the registered or principal office of the third country entity` THEN JUST "the registered or principal office of the third country entity"
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(4)(a) another item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- reg 45ZA(4)(b): within 90 days of acquiring an interest in a third country entity afterwards.
-- src:1530 | (4) The trustees of a trust to which paragraph (1) ... applies must—
-- src:1531 | (a) if they have a controlling interest in a third country entity, provide the Commissioners with the following information, apart from any information already provided under regulation 45(10G), at the same time as providing the information under paragraph (3)—
-- src:1532 | (i) the third country entity’s corporate or firm name;
-- src:1533 | (ii) the country or territory by whose law the third country entity is governed;
-- src:1534 | (iii) the registered or principal office of the third country entity;
-- src:1535 | (b) if they acquire an interest in a third country entity after providing the information under paragraph (3), provide the Commissioners with the information specified in this paragraph within 90 days of the date on which they acquired that interest.
@ref reg 45ZA(4) (src:1530-1535)
GIVEN `the date on which the trustees acquired the interest in the third country entity` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45ZA(4)(b) the last day for providing the information` MEANS `the date on which the trustees acquired the interest in the third country entity` PLUS 90

-- reg 45ZA(5): the day by which the (3) information is due.
DECLARE `reg 45ZA(5) basis` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZA(5) the trust first falls within paragraph (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (c)(i)`
    `reg 45ZA(5)(aa) the trust falls within paragraph (1)(b)(iii) or (c)(ii)`

-- src:1536 | (5) The information required under paragraph (3) must be provided—
-- src:1537 | (a) on or before 1st September 2022, in the case of a trust which first falls within paragraph (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (c)(i) before 4th June 2022;
-- src:1538 | (aa) on or before 1st September 2027, in the case of a trust which falls within paragraph (1)(b)(iii) or (c)(ii);
-- src:1539 | (b) in any other case, within 90 days of the trust being set up, or, if later, within 90 days of the trust first falling within paragraph (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (c)(i).
@ref reg 45ZA(5) (src:1536-1539)
GIVEN basis IS A `reg 45ZA(5) basis`
      `the date on which the trust was set up` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the trust first fell within paragraph (1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45ZA(5) the last day for providing the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(5)(aa) the trust falls within paragraph (1)(b)(iii) or (c)(ii)` THEN Date 1 9 2027
    WHEN `reg 45ZA(5) the trust first falls within paragraph (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (c)(i)` THEN
        IF `the date on which the trust first fell within paragraph (1)` LESS THAN Date 4 6 2022
        THEN Date 1 9 2022
        ELSE (`mlr2 the later of two days` `the date on which the trust was set up` `the date on which the trust first fell within paragraph (1)`) PLUS 90

-- src:1536 | (5) The information required under paragraph (3) must be provided—
-- src:1537 | (a) on or before 1st September 2022, in the case of a trust which first falls within paragraph (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (c)(i) before 4th June 2022;
-- src:1538 | (aa) on or before 1st September 2027, in the case of a trust which falls within paragraph (1)(b)(iii) or (c)(ii);
-- src:1539 | (b) in any other case, within 90 days of the trust being set up, or, if later, within 90 days of the trust first falling within paragraph (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (c)(i).
@ref reg 45ZA(5) (src:1536-1539)
GIVEN `the date on which the information was provided` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day for providing the information` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(5) the information was provided in time` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the information was provided` `the last day for providing the information` `the date asked`

-- reg 45ZA(6): a change, within 90 days of the trustee becoming aware.
-- src:1540 | (6) If a trustee becomes aware that any of the information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (3) or (4) has changed, the trustee must notify the Commissioners of the change within 90 days of the trustee becoming aware of the change.
@ref reg 45ZA(6) (src:1540-1540)
GIVEN `reg 45ZA(1) the information to be contained in the register is the information referred to in paragraphs (3) and (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a trustee becomes aware that information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (3) or (4) has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(6) the trustee must notify the Commissioners of the change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `mlr2 within the scope` `reg 45ZA(1) the information to be contained in the register is the information referred to in paragraphs (3) and (4)` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of the trustees of a trust to which paragraph (1) applies
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `a trustee becomes aware that information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (3) or (4) has changed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a trustee becomes aware that any of the information ... has changed, the trustee must notify" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:1540 | (6) If a trustee becomes aware that any of the information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (3) or (4) has changed, the trustee must notify the Commissioners of the change within 90 days of the trustee becoming aware of the change.
@ref reg 45ZA(6) (src:1540-1540)
GIVEN `the date on which the trustee became aware of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45ZA(6) the last day for the notification` MEANS `the date on which the trustee became aware of the change` PLUS 90

-- src:1540 | (6) If a trustee becomes aware that any of the information provided to the Commissioners under paragraph (3) or (4) has changed, the trustee must notify the Commissioners of the change within 90 days of the trustee becoming aware of the change.
@ref reg 45ZA(6) (src:1540-1540)
GIVEN `the date on which the notification was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the trustee became aware of the change` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(6) the notification was given within 90 days` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the notification was given` (`reg 45ZA(6) the last day for the notification` `the date on which the trustee became aware of the change`) `the date asked`

DECLARE `reg 45ZA(6) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZA(6) a trustee of a trust to which paragraph (1) applies`

DECLARE `reg 45ZA(6) act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZA(6) notify the Commissioners of the change`

@ref reg 45ZA(6) (src:1540-1540)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 45ZA(6) party` `reg 45ZA(6) act`
`reg 45ZA(6) the trustee must notify the Commissioners within 90 days` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 45ZA(6) a trustee of a trust to which paragraph (1) applies`
    MUST `reg 45ZA(6) notify the Commissioners of the change`
    WITHIN 90
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the trustee did not notify the Commissioners of the change within 90 days of becoming aware of the change"

-- reg 45ZA(7)
-- src:1541 | (7) The information required under paragraphs (3), (4) and (6) must be provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require.
@ref reg 45ZA(7) (src:1541-1541)
GIVEN `the information was provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZA(7) the information required under paragraphs (3), (4) and (6) was provided in the form required` MEANS
    IF `the information was provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be provided in such form as the Commissioners reasonably require" (a "must" not discharged, marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

§§ `Regulation 45ZB -- Access to information on the register`

-- src:1567 | (9) The details are, in relation to an individual—
-- src:1568 | (a) the individual’s full name;
-- src:1569 | (b) the individual’s month and year of birth;
-- src:1570 | (c) the individual’s country of residence;
-- src:1571 | (d) the individual’s nationality;
-- src:1572 | (e) the nature and extent of the individual’s beneficial interest.
@ref reg 45ZB(9) (src:1567-1572)
DECLARE `reg 45ZB(9) detail` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZB(9)(a) the individual's full name`
    `reg 45ZB(9)(b) the individual's month and year of birth`
    `reg 45ZB(9)(c) the individual's country of residence`
    `reg 45ZB(9)(d) the individual's nationality`
    `reg 45ZB(9)(e) the nature and extent of the individual's beneficial interest`
    `reg 45ZB(9) another detail`

@ref reg 45ZB(9) (src:1567-1572)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 45ZB(9) detail`
`reg 45ZB(9) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 45ZB(9)(a) the individual's full name`
    , `reg 45ZB(9)(b) the individual's month and year of birth`
    , `reg 45ZB(9)(c) the individual's country of residence`
    , `reg 45ZB(9)(d) the individual's nationality`
    , `reg 45ZB(9)(e) the nature and extent of the individual's beneficial interest`

-- reg 45ZB(9): the details about an individual that are accessible information.
@ref reg 45ZB(9) (src:1567-1572)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZB(9) detail`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(9) the item is an accessible detail about an individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(a) the individual's full name` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "The details are, in relation to an individual"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(b) the individual's month and year of birth` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "The details are, in relation to an individual"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(c) the individual's country of residence` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "The details are, in relation to an individual"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(d) the individual's nationality` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "The details are, in relation to an individual"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(e) the nature and extent of the individual's beneficial interest` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "The details are, in relation to an individual"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9) another detail` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 45ZB(8) says the accessible information "means the details specified in paragraph (9) or (10)" and paragraph (9) says "The details are"; a detail in none of the heads is not accessible information (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated definitions (a))

@ref reg 45ZB(9) (src:1567-1572)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZB(9) detail`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 45ZB(9) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(a) the individual's full name` THEN JUST "the individual’s full name"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(b) the individual's month and year of birth` THEN JUST "the individual’s month and year of birth"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(c) the individual's country of residence` THEN JUST "the individual’s country of residence"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(d) the individual's nationality` THEN JUST "the individual’s nationality"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9)(e) the nature and extent of the individual's beneficial interest` THEN JUST "the nature and extent of the individual’s beneficial interest"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(9) another detail` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- src:1573 | (10) The details are, in relation to a legal entity—
-- src:1574 | (a) the legal entity’s corporate or firm name;
-- src:1575 | (b) the registered or principal office of the legal entity;
-- src:1576 | (c) the nature of the entity’s role in relation to the trust.
@ref reg 45ZB(10) (src:1573-1576)
DECLARE `reg 45ZB(10) detail` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZB(10)(a) the legal entity's corporate or firm name`
    `reg 45ZB(10)(b) the registered or principal office of the legal entity`
    `reg 45ZB(10)(c) the nature of the entity's role in relation to the trust`
    `reg 45ZB(10) another detail`

@ref reg 45ZB(10) (src:1573-1576)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 45ZB(10) detail`
`reg 45ZB(10) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 45ZB(10)(a) the legal entity's corporate or firm name`
    , `reg 45ZB(10)(b) the registered or principal office of the legal entity`
    , `reg 45ZB(10)(c) the nature of the entity's role in relation to the trust`

-- reg 45ZB(10): the details about a legal entity that are accessible information.
@ref reg 45ZB(10) (src:1573-1576)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZB(10) detail`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(10) the item is an accessible detail about a legal entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(10)(a) the legal entity's corporate or firm name` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "The details are, in relation to a legal entity"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(10)(b) the registered or principal office of the legal entity` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "The details are, in relation to a legal entity"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(10)(c) the nature of the entity's role in relation to the trust` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "The details are, in relation to a legal entity"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(10) another detail` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 45ZB(8) says the accessible information "means the details specified in paragraph (9) or (10)" and paragraph (10) says "The details are"; a detail in none of the heads is not accessible information (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated definitions (a))

@ref reg 45ZB(10) (src:1573-1576)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZB(10) detail`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 45ZB(10) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(10)(a) the legal entity's corporate or firm name` THEN JUST "the legal entity’s corporate or firm name"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(10)(b) the registered or principal office of the legal entity` THEN JUST "the registered or principal office of the legal entity"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(10)(c) the nature of the entity's role in relation to the trust` THEN JUST "the nature of the entity’s role in relation to the trust"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(10) another detail` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- reg 45ZB(8): accessible information.  A definition ("means"): the details of (9) or (10), held on the register, about the persons named.
-- src:1566 | (8) For the purposes of this regulation, the “accessible information” means the details specified in paragraph (9) or (10) which are held on the register in relation to a beneficial owner of a type A trust , a type B trust or a type C trust (within the meaning given in regulation 45ZA(2)), or in relation to an individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes.
@ref reg 45ZB(8) (src:1566-1566)
GIVEN `the details are specified in paragraph (9) or (10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the details are held on the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the details relate to a beneficial owner of a type A, type B or type C trust, or to an individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(8) the details are accessible information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the details are specified in paragraph (9) or (10)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the details are held on the register` AND `the details relate to a beneficial owner of a type A, type B or type C trust, or to an individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the 'accessible information' means the details specified in paragraph (9) or (10) which are held on the register in relation to a beneficial owner of a type A trust, a type B trust or a type C trust, or in relation to an individual referred to as a potential beneficiary"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the 'accessible information' means the details specified in paragraph (9) or (10)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the details are specified in paragraph (9) or (10) has not been answered

-- reg 45ZB(5): the exemption.
DECLARE `reg 45ZB(5) ground` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZB(5)(a) making the information available would expose the beneficial owner to a disproportionate risk of fraud, kidnapping, blackmail, extortion, harassment, violence or intimidation`
    `reg 45ZB(5)(b) the beneficial owner is under the age of 18`
    `reg 45ZB(5)(c)(i) the beneficial owner lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005`
    `reg 45ZB(5)(c)(ii) the beneficial owner is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000`
    `reg 45ZB(5)(c)(iii) the beneficial owner is incapable by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986`
    `reg 45ZB(5) another ground`

-- src:1552 | (5) Paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information in a case where, and to the extent that, the Commissioners consider that the information should be exempt because—
-- src:1553 | (a) the Commissioners consider that making the information available would expose the beneficial owner to a disproportionate risk of fraud, kidnapping, blackmail, extortion, harassment, violence or intimidation;
-- src:1554 | (b) the beneficial owner is under the age of 18; or
-- src:1555 | (c) the beneficial owner—
-- src:1556 | (i) lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005;
-- src:1557 | (ii) is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000; or
-- src:1558 | (iii) is incapable by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986,
-- src:1559 | and in this paragraph, references to the beneficial owner include references to any other individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes.
@ref reg 45ZB(5) (src:1552-1559)
GIVEN `the Commissioners consider that the information should be exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `reg 45ZB(5) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(5) paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Commissioners consider that the information should be exempt`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply ... in a case where, and to the extent that, the Commissioners consider that the information should be exempt" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    ELSE CONSIDER ground
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(5)(a) making the information available would expose the beneficial owner to a disproportionate risk of fraud, kidnapping, blackmail, extortion, harassment, violence or intimidation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(5)(b) the beneficial owner is under the age of 18` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(5)(c)(i) the beneficial owner lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(5)(c)(ii) the beneficial owner is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(5)(c)(iii) the beneficial owner is incapable by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(5) another ground` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case where, and to the extent that, the Commissioners consider that the information should be exempt because (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." -- a "where" that names its grounds; a ground not listed does not bring paragraphs (1) and (3) to an end (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- reg 45ZB(5)(b): the age of the beneficial owner.  The ground is "the beneficial owner is under the age of 18".
-- src:1554 | (b) the beneficial owner is under the age of 18; or
@ref reg 45ZB(5)(b) (src:1554-1554)
GIVEN `the age of the beneficial owner, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(5)(b) the age of the beneficial owner meets the ground` MEANS
    IF `the age of the beneficial owner, in years` LESS THAN 18
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the beneficial owner is under the age of 18" -- a beneficial owner aged 18 or more does not meet the ground

-- reg 45ZB(1): the Commissioners must make the accessible information available.
-- src:1543 | (1) The Commissioners must make the accessible information available to a person who demonstrates to the Commissioners a legitimate interest in the beneficial ownership of a trust, where that person so requests.
@ref reg 45ZB(1) (src:1543-1543)
GIVEN `the person demonstrates to the Commissioners a legitimate interest in the beneficial ownership of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person so requests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 45ZB(5) paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(1) the Commissioners must make the accessible information available to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person so requests`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where that person so requests" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF (NOT `the person demonstrates to the Commissioners a legitimate interest in the beneficial ownership of a trust`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person who demonstrates to the Commissioners a legitimate interest in the beneficial ownership of a trust"
        IF `reg 45ZB(5) paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information in a case where, and to the extent that, the Commissioners consider that the information should be exempt"
        IF `reg 45ZB(5) paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (5) exempts the information has not been answered

-- reg 45ZB(2): information to a trustee, so that a relevant person can meet its obligations under Part 3.
-- SEAM S-1 (asking)
-- src:1544 | (2) The Commissioners must make available to a trustee, on a request by that trustee, such information as the trustee reasonably requires in order to enable a relevant person to meet the relevant person’s obligations under Part 3, where that relevant person proposes to—
-- src:1545 | (a) form a business relationship with the trust; or
-- src:1546 | (b) enter into a transaction with the trust in relation to which the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27.
@ref reg 45ZB(2) (src:1544-1546)
GIVEN `the trustee requests the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person proposes to form a business relationship with the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person proposes to enter into a transaction with the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(2) the Commissioners must make available to the trustee the information that the trustee reasonably requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the trustee requests the information`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on a request by that trustee"
        IF `the relevant person proposes to form a business relationship with the trust`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the relevant person proposes to enter into a transaction with the trust` AND `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the relevant person proposes to enter into a transaction with the trust` AND `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulation 27 requires customer due diligence measures has not been answered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where that relevant person proposes to (a) form a business relationship with the trust; or (b) enter into a transaction with the trust in relation to which the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- reg 45ZB(3): a written request about a type A, B or C trust whose trustees have a controlling interest in a third country entity.
-- src:1547 | (3) The Commissioners must make the accessible information available to a person who makes a written request about a type A trust , a type B trust or a type C trust (within the meaning given in regulation 45ZA(2)), where the trustees of that trust have a controlling interest in a third country entity.
@ref reg 45ZB(3) (src:1547-1547)
GIVEN `the person makes a written request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is about a type A trust, a type B trust or a type C trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(6)(a) the trustees have a controlling interest in a third country entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 45ZB(5) paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(3) the Commissioners must make the accessible information available to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person makes a written request`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person who makes a written request"
        IF `reg 45ZB(5) paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information in a case where, and to the extent that, the Commissioners consider that the information should be exempt"
        IF `mlr2 both are true` `the request is about a type A trust, a type B trust or a type C trust` `reg 42(6)(a) the trustees have a controlling interest in a third country entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN (IF `reg 45ZB(5) paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (5) exempts the information has not been answered
        IF `mlr2 both are true` `the request is about a type A trust, a type B trust or a type C trust` `reg 42(6)(a) the trustees have a controlling interest in a third country entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the trustees of that trust have a controlling interest in a third country entity" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer the rule depends on has not been given

-- reg 45ZB(4): what the Commissioners may do about a request under (1) or (3).
-- src:1548 | (4) The Commissioners may—
-- src:1549 | (a) charge a fee to any person making a request for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3), which must not exceed such amount as the Commissioners consider will enable them to meet any expenses reasonably incurred by them in dealing with such requests, including expenses incurred in maintaining the register;
-- src:1550 | (b) require the person to submit the request in such a manner as the Commissioners may reasonably require, including by requiring the person to register in a manner specified by the Commissioners; and
-- src:1551 | (c) require the person to provide such information to support the request as the Commissioners may specify.
@ref reg 45ZB(4) (src:1548-1551)
GIVEN `the request is for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that the Commissioners consider will enable them to meet any expenses reasonably incurred by them in dealing with such requests, including expenses incurred in maintaining the register, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(4)(a) the Commissioners may charge the fee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the request is for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a fee to any person making a request for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3)"
        IF `the fee, in pounds` AT MOST `the amount that the Commissioners consider will enable them to meet any expenses reasonably incurred by them in dealing with such requests, including expenses incurred in maintaining the register, in pounds`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must not exceed such amount as the Commissioners consider will enable them to meet any expenses reasonably incurred"

-- src:1548 | (4) The Commissioners may—
-- src:1549 | (a) charge a fee to any person making a request for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3), which must not exceed such amount as the Commissioners consider will enable them to meet any expenses reasonably incurred by them in dealing with such requests, including expenses incurred in maintaining the register;
-- src:1550 | (b) require the person to submit the request in such a manner as the Commissioners may reasonably require, including by requiring the person to register in a manner specified by the Commissioners; and
-- src:1551 | (c) require the person to provide such information to support the request as the Commissioners may specify.
@ref reg 45ZB(4) (src:1548-1551)
GIVEN `the request is for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner is one that the Commissioners may reasonably require, including requiring the person to register in a manner specified by the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(4)(b) the Commissioners may require the person to submit the request in the manner` MEANS
    IF `the request is for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3)` AND `the manner is one that the Commissioners may reasonably require, including requiring the person to register in a manner specified by the Commissioners`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in such a manner as the Commissioners may reasonably require, including by requiring the person to register in a manner specified by the Commissioners"

-- src:1548 | (4) The Commissioners may—
-- src:1549 | (a) charge a fee to any person making a request for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3), which must not exceed such amount as the Commissioners consider will enable them to meet any expenses reasonably incurred by them in dealing with such requests, including expenses incurred in maintaining the register;
-- src:1550 | (b) require the person to submit the request in such a manner as the Commissioners may reasonably require, including by requiring the person to register in a manner specified by the Commissioners; and
-- src:1551 | (c) require the person to provide such information to support the request as the Commissioners may specify.
@ref reg 45ZB(4) (src:1548-1551)
GIVEN `the request is for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is information to support the request that the Commissioners may specify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(4)(c) the Commissioners may require the person to provide the information to support the request` MEANS
    IF `the request is for accessible information under paragraph (1) or (3)` AND `the information is information to support the request that the Commissioners may specify`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such information to support the request as the Commissioners may specify"

-- reg 45ZB(6): the notice of an exemption decision.  The period for seeking a review must be at least 30 days from the day the person is informed.
-- src:1560 | (6) Where the Commissioners decide to exempt any of the accessible information in accordance with paragraph (5), the Commissioners must inform the person requesting the information of the decision, explain that the person is entitled to seek a review, and specify the period in which the person must inform the Commissioners that the person wishes to seek a review (which must not be less than 30 days beginning with the day on which the person is informed of the decision).
@ref reg 45ZB(6) (src:1560-1560)
GIVEN `the number of days in the period specified for seeking a review, beginning with the day on which the person is informed of the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(6) the period specified for seeking a review is long enough` MEANS
    IF `the number of days in the period specified for seeking a review, beginning with the day on which the person is informed of the decision` AT LEAST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(which must not be less than 30 days beginning with the day on which the person is informed of the decision)"

-- The earliest end of the period: "not less than 30 days beginning with the day on which the person is informed".  The day of the information is day 1 (fork F45ZB-1).
-- src:1560 | (6) Where the Commissioners decide to exempt any of the accessible information in accordance with paragraph (5), the Commissioners must inform the person requesting the information of the decision, explain that the person is entitled to seek a review, and specify the period in which the person must inform the Commissioners that the person wishes to seek a review (which must not be less than 30 days beginning with the day on which the person is informed of the decision).
@ref reg 45ZB(6) (src:1560-1560)
GIVEN `the day on which the person is informed of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45ZB(6) the earliest last day of the period specified for seeking a review` MEANS `the day on which the person is informed of the decision` PLUS 29

-- src:1560 | (6) Where the Commissioners decide to exempt any of the accessible information in accordance with paragraph (5), the Commissioners must inform the person requesting the information of the decision, explain that the person is entitled to seek a review, and specify the period in which the person must inform the Commissioners that the person wishes to seek a review (which must not be less than 30 days beginning with the day on which the person is informed of the decision).
@ref reg 45ZB(6) (src:1560-1560)
GIVEN `the day on which the person is informed of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period specified for seeking a review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(6) the last day specified is late enough` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the period specified for seeking a review` AT LEAST `reg 45ZB(6) the earliest last day of the period specified for seeking a review` `the day on which the person is informed of the decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must not be less than 30 days beginning with the day on which the person is informed of the decision" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:1560 | (6) Where the Commissioners decide to exempt any of the accessible information in accordance with paragraph (5), the Commissioners must inform the person requesting the information of the decision, explain that the person is entitled to seek a review, and specify the period in which the person must inform the Commissioners that the person wishes to seek a review (which must not be less than 30 days beginning with the day on which the person is informed of the decision).
@ref reg 45ZB(6) (src:1560-1560)
GIVEN `the Commissioners decide to exempt any of the accessible information in accordance with paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they inform the person requesting the information of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they explain that the person is entitled to seek a review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they specify the period in which the person must inform them that the person wishes to seek a review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(6) the Commissioners have given the notice of the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Commissioners decide to exempt any of the accessible information in accordance with paragraph (5)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Commissioners decide to exempt any of the accessible information in accordance with paragraph (5), the Commissioners must inform" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `they inform the person requesting the information of the decision` AND `they explain that the person is entitled to seek a review` AND `they specify the period in which the person must inform them that the person wishes to seek a review`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commissioners must inform the person requesting the information of the decision, explain that the person is entitled to seek a review, and specify the period" (a "must" not discharged, marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 45ZB(7): the outcomes of a review.
DECLARE `reg 45ZB(7) decision` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZB(7)(a) uphold the decision to exempt the information`
    `reg 45ZB(7)(b) make the information available`
    `reg 45ZB(7)(c) exempt less of the requested information and make more of the requested information available`
    `reg 45ZB(7) another decision`

-- src:1561 | (7) If the person seeks a review, the Commissioners may decide to—
-- src:1562 | (a) uphold the decision to exempt the information;
-- src:1563 | (b) make the information available; or
-- src:1564 | (c) exempt less of the requested information and make more of the requested information available,
-- src:1565 | and must inform the person who made the request of their decision.
@ref reg 45ZB(7) (src:1561-1565)
GIVEN `the person seeks a review` IS A BOOLEAN
      decision IS A `reg 45ZB(7) decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(7) the Commissioners may decide` MEANS
    IF `the person seeks a review`
    THEN CONSIDER decision
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(7)(a) uphold the decision to exempt the information` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(7)(b) make the information available` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(7)(c) exempt less of the requested information and make more of the requested information available` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 45ZB(7) another decision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of the three decisions "(a) uphold ...; (b) make the information available; or (c) exempt less"; the paragraph says nothing of any other decision
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the person seeks a review, the Commissioners may decide to" (an "if" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:1561 | (7) If the person seeks a review, the Commissioners may decide to—
-- src:1562 | (a) uphold the decision to exempt the information;
-- src:1563 | (b) make the information available; or
-- src:1564 | (c) exempt less of the requested information and make more of the requested information available,
-- src:1565 | and must inform the person who made the request of their decision.
@ref reg 45ZB(7) (src:1561-1565)
GIVEN `the person seeks a review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(7) the Commissioners must inform the person who made the request of their decision` MEANS
    IF `the person seeks a review`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the person seeks a review, the Commissioners may decide to ... and must inform the person who made the request of their decision" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)

-- src:1577 | (11) For the purposes of this regulation, the Commissioners must take account of the following when determining whether a person has a legitimate interest in the beneficial ownership of a trust—
-- src:1578 | (a) whether the person is involved in an investigation into money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing;
-- src:1579 | (b) whether the person is making the request for accessible information in order to further an investigation into a specified suspected instance of money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing;
-- src:1580 | (c) whether the disclosure of the information to that person would be likely to prejudice—
-- src:1581 | (i) any criminal investigation or criminal proceedings;
-- src:1582 | (ii) any other investigation mentioned in section 342(1) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (offences of prejudicing investigation); or
-- src:1583 | (iii) any investigation by an appropriate officer (within the meaning given in regulation 87(10)) into a potential contravention of a relevant requirement,
-- src:1584 | which is or are being, or is or are about to be, conducted;
-- src:1585 | (d) whether, having regard to the information produced by the person making the request, it is reasonable for that person to suspect that the trust is being used for money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing.
@ref reg 45ZB(11) (src:1577-1585)
DECLARE `reg 45ZB(11) matter` IS ONE OF
    `reg 45ZB(11)(a) whether the person is involved in an investigation into money`
    `reg 45ZB(11)(b) whether the person is making the request for accessible information`
    `reg 45ZB(11)(c) whether the disclosure of the information to that person would be`
    `reg 45ZB(11)(d) whether, having regard to the information produced by the person making`
    `reg 45ZB(11) another matter`

@ref reg 45ZB(11) (src:1577-1585)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 45ZB(11) matter`
`reg 45ZB(11) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 45ZB(11)(a) whether the person is involved in an investigation into money`
    , `reg 45ZB(11)(b) whether the person is making the request for accessible information`
    , `reg 45ZB(11)(c) whether the disclosure of the information to that person would be`
    , `reg 45ZB(11)(d) whether, having regard to the information produced by the person making`

-- reg 45ZB(11): the matters the Commissioners must take into account in deciding whether a person has a legitimate interest.
@ref reg 45ZB(11) (src:1577-1585)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZB(11) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 45ZB(11) the Commissioners must take the matter into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11)(a) whether the person is involved in an investigation into money` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of the following"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11)(b) whether the person is making the request for accessible information` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of the following"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11)(c) whether the disclosure of the information to that person would be` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of the following"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11)(d) whether, having regard to the information produced by the person making` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of the following"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists the matters and does not close the list

@ref reg 45ZB(11) (src:1577-1585)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 45ZB(11) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 45ZB(11) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11)(a) whether the person is involved in an investigation into money` THEN JUST "whether the person is involved in an investigation into money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11)(b) whether the person is making the request for accessible information` THEN JUST "whether the person is making the request for accessible information in order to further an investigation into a specified suspected instance of money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11)(c) whether the disclosure of the information to that person would be` THEN JUST "whether the disclosure of the information to that person would be likely to prejudice— (i) any criminal investigation or criminal proceedings; (ii) any other investigation mentioned in section 342(1) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (offences of prejudicing investigation); or (iii) any investigation by an appropriate officer (within the meaning given in regulation 87(10)) into a potential contravention of a relevant requirement, which is or are being, or is or are about to be, conducted"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11)(d) whether, having regard to the information produced by the person making` THEN JUST "whether, having regard to the information produced by the person making the request, it is reasonable for that person to suspect that the trust is being used for money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing"
    WHEN `reg 45ZB(11) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list
